{
  "schema": "zetesis.refinement.evaluation.check.v1",
  "checkedOn": "2026-10-03",
  "scope": "The extracted scalar reference checker is refined under fixed-observation and scalar/sequence models. Generated owner checks and cloning obey explicit immutable-heap contracts. Actual zero initialization establishes the empty packed subset. These operations compose with original evaluation, root checking, atom selection and completed proper-subset search to decide answer-set membership under explicit admission and storage premises. Actual failed roots and returned countermodels exclude membership. Typed interruptions do not establish a Boolean verdict. A separate checked event model permits changing observations and fallible reservation; it is not installed in the extracted checker. The generated admission step called by Theory::new computes the authored validator, including the dimension and padded-count checks, and returns the supplied data unchanged; its node and root validators compute the authored scans for every represented slice, and a node refusal reports the error of the first refused node. Data returned by the admission step supplies the ordered-children and bounded-root premises, which remain premises of the composed theorems. Public allocation/setup, changing runtime observations, grounding, solver enumeration and GPU execution remain outside this proof.",
